ER Diagram (Entities + Relationships)
Entities

users

roles (optional; can be enum instead)

categories

properties

property_images (for multiple images)

inquiries (booking/visit request / contact agent)

favorites (user wishlist)

property_status_logs (optional auditing)

Relationships (Cardinality)

Category (1) → (M) Properties

User (Agent) (1) → (M) Properties

Property (1) → (M) PropertyImages

User (Customer) (1) → (M) Inquiries

Property (1) → (M) Inquiries

User (Agent) (1) → (M) Inquiries (inquiry is sent to agent)

User (Customer) (M) ↔ (M) Property through favorites

Normalized Tables (3NF)
1) users

Stores all system users (Admin/Agent/User).

Field	Type	Key	Notes
id	bigint	PK	
name	varchar(100)		
email	varchar(150)	UQ	
phone	varchar(30)		nullable
role	enum('admin','agent','user')		(or role_id FK)
password	varchar(255)		hashed
status	enum('active','blocked')		optional
email_verified_at	timestamp		nullable
remember_token	varchar(100)		nullable
created_at	timestamp		
updated_at	timestamp		

✅ 3NF: all attributes depend on user id only.

2) categories
Field	Type	Key	Notes
id	bigint	PK	
name	varchar(80)	UQ	e.g. Apartment, Villa
slug	varchar(120)	UQ	
created_at / updated_at	timestamp		
3) properties

Core listing table.

Field	Type	Key	Notes
id	bigint	PK	
category_id	bigint	FK	→ categories.id
agent_id	bigint	FK	→ users.id (role=agent)
title	varchar(150)		
description	text		
price	decimal(12,2)		
area_sqft	int		nullable
bedrooms	tinyint		nullable
bathrooms	tinyint		nullable
address	varchar(255)		
city	varchar(80)		
state	varchar(80)		nullable
pincode	varchar(12)		nullable
latitude	decimal(10,7)		nullable
longitude	decimal(10,7)		nullable
main_image	varchar(255)		optional if using property_images
status	enum('active','inactive','pending')		
created_at / updated_at	timestamp		

✅ 3NF: property data depends only on property id. Agent and category are referenced via FK.

4) property_images

(If you want multiple images per property)

Field	Type	Key	Notes
id	bigint	PK	
property_id	bigint	FK	→ properties.id
image_path	varchar(255)		
is_primary	boolean		default 0
created_at / updated_at	timestamp		

✅ avoids repeating image columns in properties (normalization).

5) inquiries

User inquiry / booking request to agent for a property.

Field	Type	Key	Notes
id	bigint	PK	
property_id	bigint	FK	→ properties.id
user_id	bigint	FK	→ users.id (role=user)
agent_id	bigint	FK	→ users.id (role=agent)
name	varchar(100)		
email	varchar(150)		
phone	varchar(30)		nullable
message	text		nullable
visit_date	date		nullable (optional)
status	enum('pending','replied','closed')		
created_at / updated_at	timestamp		

✅ 3NF: inquiry depends on inquiry id; property/user/agent are FKs.

6) favorites

Many-to-many: Users can favorite many properties.

Field	Type	Key	Notes
id	bigint	PK	
user_id	bigint	FK	→ users.id
property_id	bigint	FK	→ properties.id
created_at / updated_at	timestamp		

Constraints:

Unique(user_id, property_id) ✅ prevents duplicate favorites

7) property_status_logs (Optional, real-world auditing)

Tracks changes like active → inactive.

Field	Type	Key	Notes
id	bigint	PK	
property_id	bigint	FK	
changed_by	bigint	FK	→ users.id
old_status	varchar(20)		
new_status	varchar(20)		
note	varchar(255)		nullable
created_at	timestamp		
